{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"According to the Mean Value Theorem, there exists a number $c$ in the open interval $1\u003cx\u003c3$ such that $f'(c)$ is equal to the average rate of change of $f$ over the interval:\n\n$f'(c)=\\dfrac{f(3)-f(1)}{(3)-(1)}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"First, let's find that average rate of change:\n\n$\\dfrac{f(3)-f(1)}{(3)-(1)}=\\dfrac{3-1}{2}=\\blueD{1}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Now, let's differentiate $f$ and find the $x$-value for which $f'(x)=\\blueD{1}$.\n\n$f'(x)=\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{4x-3}}$ [[☃ explanation 1]]\n\nThe solution of $f'(x)=1$ is $x=1.75$.  [[☃ explanation 2]]\n\n$x=1.75$ is indeed within the interval $1\u003cx\u003c3$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nf'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}{\\sqrt{4x-3}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(4x-3)^{\\large\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2}(4x-3)^{\\large -\\frac{1}{2}}\\dfrac{d}{dx}(4x-3)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{4x-3}}(4)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{4x-3}}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}},"explanation 2":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nf'(x)\u0026=1\n\\\\\\\\\n\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{4x-3}}\u0026=1\n\\\\\\\\\n\\sqrt{4x-3}\u0026=2\n\\\\\\\\\n(\\sqrt{4x-3})^2\u0026=2^2\n\\\\\\\\\n4x-3\u0026=4\n\\\\\\\\\n4x\u0026=7\n\\\\\\\\\nx\u0026=1.75\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $c=1.75$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $f(x)=\\sqrt{4x-3}$ and let $c$ be the number that satisfies the Mean Value Theorem for $f$ on the interval $1\\leq x\\leq3$.\n\n**What is $c$ ?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$1.5$","correct":false},{"content":"$1.75$","correct":true},{"content":"$2$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$2.25$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
